examples.question_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.36]
\draw (0,0)--(13,0)--(13,4)--(5,4)--(5,11)--(0,11)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0,4)--(5,4);
\node[below] at (6.5,0) {$13\text{ cm}$};
\node[right] at (13,2) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\node[above] at (2.5,11) {$5\text{ cm}$};
\node[left] at (0,5.5) {$11\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
All angles are right angles. Find the area of the L-shape in two different ways.

examples.solution_text:
The upper rectangle has height $11-4=7\text{ cm}$. Split along the dashed line.
$\begin{align*} A&=13\times4+5\times7\\ &=52+35\\ &=87\text{ cm}^2 \end{align*}$
Alternatively, split vertically. The lower-right rectangle has width $13-5=8\text{ cm}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.36]
\draw (0,0)--(13,0)--(13,4)--(5,4)--(5,11)--(0,11)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (5,0)--(5,4);
\node at (2.5,5.5) {$A_1$};
\node at (9,2) {$A_2$};
\node[below] at (2.5,0) {$5\text{ cm}$};
\node[below] at (9,0) {$8\text{ cm}$};
\node[left] at (0,5.5) {$11\text{ cm}$};
\node[right] at (13,2) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*} A&=5\times11+8\times4\\ &=55+32\\ &=87\text{ cm}^2 \end{align*}$
Both ways count the whole shape once.

