[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.42]
\draw (0,0)--(9,0)--(9,4)--(3,10)--(0,4)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0,4)--(9,4);
\draw[dashed] (3,4)--(3,10);
\draw (3,4.35)--(3.35,4.35)--(3.35,4);
\node[below] at (4.5,0) {$9\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,2) {$4\text{ m}$};
\draw[thin] (9,0)--(11,0);
\draw[thin] (3,10)--(11,10);
\draw[<->] (10.5,0)--(10.5,10) node[midway,right] {$10\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The figure is a rectangle with a triangle on top. Calculate its area.

examples.solution_text:
Triangle height: $10-4=6\text{ m}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.42]
\draw (0,0)--(9,0)--(9,4)--(3,10)--(0,4)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0,4)--(9,4);
\draw[dashed] (3,4)--(3,10) node[midway,right] {$6\text{ m}$};
\draw (3,4.35)--(3.35,4.35)--(3.35,4);
\node at (4.5,2) {$A_1$};
\node at (4.8,5.3) {$A_2$};
\node[below] at (4.5,0) {$9\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,2) {$4\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Rectangle area:
$\begin{align*} A_1&=9\times4\\ &=36\text{ m}^2 \end{align*}$
Triangle area:
$\begin{align*} A_2&=9\times6\div2\\ &=54\div2\\ &=27\text{ m}^2 \end{align*}$
$\begin{align*} A&=A_1+A_2\\ &=36+27\\ &=63\text{ m}^2 \end{align*}$

