An L-shaped room has all right angles. Its total height is $300\text{ cm}$ and its upper section is $150\text{ cm}$ wide. The lower section extends $7\text{ m}$ beyond the upper section and is $2\text{ m}$ high. Find the floor area in $\text{m}^2$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.55]
\draw (0,0)--(8.5,0)--(8.5,2)--(1.5,2)--(1.5,3)--(0,3)--cycle;
\node[left] at (0,1.5) {$300\text{ cm}$};
\node[above] at (0.75,3) {$150\text{ cm}$};
\node[above] at (5,2) {$7\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (8.5,1) {$2\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Use metres for all lengths: $300\text{ cm}=3\text{ m}$ and $150\text{ cm}=1.5\text{ m}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.55]
\draw (0,0)--(8.5,0)--(8.5,2)--(1.5,2)--(1.5,3)--(0,3)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (1.5,0)--(1.5,2);
\node at (0.75,1.5) {$A_1$};
\node at (5,1) {$A_2$};
\node[left] at (0,1.5) {$3\text{ m}$};
\node[above] at (0.75,3) {$1.5\text{ m}$};
\node[above] at (5,2) {$7\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (8.5,1) {$2\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The first rectangle covers the full height.
$\begin{align*} A_1&=1.5\times3\\ &=4.5\text{ m}^2 \end{align*}$
The lower extension is a separate rectangle.
$\begin{align*} A_2&=7\times2\\ &=14\text{ m}^2 \end{align*}$
$\begin{align*} A&=A_1+A_2\\ &=4.5+14\\ &=18.5\text{ m}^2 \end{align*}$

examples.question_text:
All angles are right angles. Find the area by subtracting the missing corner from the surrounding rectangle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.4]
\draw (0,0)--(12,0)--(12,5)--(8,5)--(8,9)--(0,9)--cycle;
\node[below] at (6,0) {$12\text{ cm}$};
\node[left] at (0,4.5) {$9\text{ cm}$};
\node[right] at (12,2.5) {$5\text{ cm}$};
\node[above] at (10,5) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The missing rectangle has height $9-5=4\text{ cm}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.4]
\draw (0,0)--(12,0)--(12,5)--(8,5)--(8,9)--(0,9)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (12,5)--(12,9)--(8,9);
\node[below] at (6,0) {$12\text{ cm}$};
\node[left] at (0,4.5) {$9\text{ cm}$};
\node[above] at (10,9) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\node[right] at (12,7) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\node at (4,4) {$A_1$};
\node at (10,7) {$A_2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*} A&=A_1-A_2\\ &=12\times9-4\times4\\ &=108-16\\ &=92\text{ cm}^2 \end{align*}$

examples.question_text:
All angles are right angles. Find the area by splitting the figure into three rectangles.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.4]
\draw (0,0)--(12,0)--(12,4)--(8,4)--(8,7)--(4,7)--(4,10)--(0,10)--cycle;
\node[below] at (6,0) {$12\text{ cm}$};
\node[left] at (0,5) {$10\text{ cm}$};
\node[right] at (12,2) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\node[above] at (10,4) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\node[right] at (8,5.5) {$3\text{ cm}$};
\node[above] at (6,7) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\node[right] at (4,8.5) {$3\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The top width is $12-4-4=4\text{ cm}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.4]
\draw (0,0)--(12,0)--(12,4)--(8,4)--(8,7)--(4,7)--(4,10)--(0,10)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (4,0)--(4,7);
\draw[dashed] (8,0)--(8,4);
\node at (2,5) {$A_1$};
\node at (6,3.5) {$A_2$};
\node at (10,2) {$A_3$};
\node[below] at (2,0) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\node[below] at (6,0) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\node[below] at (10,0) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\node[left] at (0,5) {$10\text{ cm}$};
\node[right] at (8,5.5) {$3\text{ cm}$};
\node[right] at (12,2) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The middle rectangle has height $4+3=7\text{ cm}$.
$\begin{align*} A&=A_1+A_2+A_3\\ &=4\times10+4\times7+4\times4\\ &=40+28+16\\ &=84\text{ cm}^2 \end{align*}$

examples.question_text:
Find each remaining area.
(a) A wall is $8\text{ m}$ long and $3\text{ m}$ high. Three separate square windows, each with side $1\text{ m}$, are cut out.
(b) Four identical corner squares are removed from a square of side $10\text{ m}$. Each removed square has side $2\text{ m}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.45]
\draw (2,0)--(8,0)--(8,2)--(10,2)--(10,8)--(8,8)--(8,10)--(2,10)--(2,8)--(0,8)--(0,2)--(2,2)--cycle;
\draw[thin] (0,2)--(0,-1.3);
\draw[thin] (10,2)--(10,-1.3);
\draw[<->] (0,-1)--(10,-1) node[midway,below] {$10\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (8,1) {$2\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
All angles in (b) are right angles.

examples.solution_text:
(a) Subtract the areas of all three windows.
$\begin{align*} A&=8\times3-3\times(1\times1)\\ &=24-3\\ &=21\text{ m}^2 \end{align*}$
(b) Complete the surrounding square, then subtract all four corner squares.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.45]
\draw (2,0)--(8,0)--(8,2)--(10,2)--(10,8)--(8,8)--(8,10)--(2,10)--(2,8)--(0,8)--(0,2)--(2,2)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0,2)--(0,0)--(2,0);
\draw[dashed] (8,0)--(10,0)--(10,2);
\draw[dashed] (10,8)--(10,10)--(8,10);
\draw[dashed] (2,10)--(0,10)--(0,8);
\draw[thin] (0,10)--(0,11.3);
\draw[thin] (10,10)--(10,11.3);
\draw[<->] (0,11)--(10,11) node[midway,above] {$10\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (10,1) {$2\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (9,0) {$2\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*} A&=10\times10-4\times(2\times2)\\ &=100-4\times4\\ &=100-16\\ &=84\text{ m}^2 \end{align*}$

examples.question_text:
A rectangular garden is $7\text{ m}$ long and $4\text{ m}$ wide. A path of constant width $1\text{ m}$ surrounds it. Find the area of the path.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.55]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (9,6);
\draw (1,1) rectangle (8,5);
\node[above] at (4.5,5) {$7\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (8,3) {$4\text{ m}$};
\node at (4.5,3) {Garden};
\draw[<->] (3,0)--(3,1) node[midway,right] {$1\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Include the path on both sides of each garden dimension.
Outer length: $7+1+1=9\text{ m}$.
Outer width: $4+1+1=6\text{ m}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.55]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (9,6);
\draw (1,1) rectangle (8,5);
\node[below] at (4.5,0) {$9\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,3) {$6\text{ m}$};
\node[above] at (4.5,5) {$7\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (8,3) {$4\text{ m}$};
\node at (4.5,3) {Garden};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*} A&=9\times6-7\times4\\ &=54-28\\ &=26\text{ m}^2 \end{align*}$
